# ==========================================
# PART 1 : AWS EC2 INSTANCE CREATION
# ==========================================

STEP 1:
Open AWS Console:
https://aws.amazon.com/console/

STEP 2:
Search: EC2

STEP 3:
Click: Launch Instance

STEP 4: CONFIGURATION

Name:
apache-server

AMI:
Ubuntu Server 22.04 LTS

Instance Type:
t2.micro

Key Pair:
Create and download mykey.pem

Security Group:
Allow:
SSH -> Port 22
HTTP -> Port 80

STEP 5:
Click Launch Instance

STEP 6:
Copy Public IP



# ==========================================
# PART 2 : WINDOWS CONNECTION (CMD / POWERSHELL)
# ==========================================

cd Downloads
dir

ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@<PUBLIC-IP>



# ==========================================
# PART 3 : UBUNTU SERVER SETUP
# ==========================================

sudo apt update

# Install Apache Web Server
sudo apt install apache2 -y

# Start Apache
sudo systemctl start apache2

# Enable Apache on boot
sudo systemctl enable apache2

# Check status
sudo systemctl status apache2



# ==========================================
# PART 4 : HOST WEBSITE
# ==========================================

cd /var/www/html

sudo nano index.html

PASTE YOUR HTML CODE (E-COMMERCE WEBSITE)



# Restart Apache
sudo systemctl restart apache2



# ==========================================
# PART 5 : OPEN WEBSITE
# ==========================================

Open Browser:

http://<PUBLIC-IP>



# ==========================================
# VIVA QUESTIONS WITH ANSWERS
# ==========================================

1. What is EC2?
EC2 is a virtual server provided by AWS used to run applications in the cloud.

2. What is Apache?
Apache is a web server software used to host websites.

3. What is Security Group?
It is a virtual firewall that controls traffic to EC2.

4. Why port 80?
It is default HTTP port for websites.

5. What is SSH?
Secure protocol to connect remote server securely.

6. What is t2.micro?
Free-tier EC2 instance used for learning.

7. What is /var/www/html?
Default Apache website directory.

8. Why restart Apache?
To apply changes made in website files.

9. Difference between start and enable?
start → runs now
enable → runs on boot

10. What is AWS?
Cloud platform providing computing services.

11. What is public IP?
IP used to access server from internet.

12. Why Apache enable?
So service starts automatically on reboot.
